{%- comment -%}
  ElmsNest v2 PDP — §4.4 "the variant / price ledger"  ·  #env2-pdp-ledger  ·  spine answer #4.

  The technical heart of the page. Every length / quantity / wattage with its own price BEFORE
  selecting, the per-metre or per-unit figure beside it, what that row is FOR (graft A), and its own
  add-to-cart. 24 variants become one decision, and the range is never hidden.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ where every number comes from
  rows      : snippets/elmsnest-v2-pdp-variants (CONTRACT-PDP §3). Captured in its default text mode —
              it PRINTS raw text, so the call is wrapped in a capture or "~~F~~" lands on the page.
              The JSON emit belongs to the stage, once per page; this section only READS that tag.
              A -> 6 rows on "אורך ומספר נורות"; C -> the PAIR עוצמה x גוון אור -> 4 rows; B -> one
              variant, so the model says mode=single and the ledger becomes a QUANTITY ledger posting
              quantity=N against the single variant id (§4.4 product B, graft C).
  per-unit  : the model's own field, computed price / metres (or / units) to the AGORA, never 1 dp.
              It is empty for a wattage axis, because a price per watt is meaningless — and it is
              suppressed on a QUANTITY ledger, where it would print the same number on every row.
  lead      : parsed VERBATIM from the product's own description — the advice paragraph that sits
              immediately before "פרטים שכדאי לדעת" (§5). Nothing is typed. Blank if nothing fits.
  headline  : two authored brand lines keyed to what the model found: the row count and unit word for
              the first, and the QUIET option's OWN NAME for the second ("הצבע לא משנה את המחיר.").
              Both are settings, so a merchant can overwrite either.
  __use     : graft A. Authored captions live in "row" BLOCKS, keyed by the option value (and
              optionally by product handle, because templates/product.elmsnest.json is shared by all
              27 products). A row with no matching block simply carries NO caption — §4.4's rule is
              "quoted, never invented", so absence is the honest state, not a placeholder.
  quiet copy: the quiet axis is printed BENEATH the table as a fact (label + values + note), and its
              describing sentence is quoted from the description when a paragraph there names at least
              two of the option's own values. It is a CONTROL only inside the no-JS row forms and in
              the JS buy line; when the axis has ONE value nothing is rendered at all (BRIEF §11).

  ------------------------------------------------------------------ no JS / JS  (the §4.4 inversion)
  NO JS  : every row visible with its price, the per-unit figure and its caption, and every row
           BUYABLE — one <form method="post" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}"> per row with the
           quiet axis as a native <select name="id">. Six prices, six forms. The strings are lit
           (the core only dims [data-lamp] under html.env2-js). Nothing needs a script.
  WITH JS: html.env2-js hides the per-row forms, the row button becomes the selector, ONE buy line
           appears under the table with the chosen row's price and a single הוספה לסל (a <button> in
           a form[data-env2-buy], so the CORE posts it to /cart/add.js and opens the cart drawer —
           §8.3: never an anchor styled as the filled pill), the stage above is driven by clicking
           its own matching stop, and ?variant= is kept in sync with history.replaceState.
           The enhanced state is the REDUCED state.
  BINDING: two-way, and that is not decoration. Until it was, the ledger and the stage could disagree
           about what the buyer had chosen — tapping "11 מ׳" on the fold rail left this section
           reading "5 מ׳" and its buy line POSTing the 5 m variant, on all three archetypes. The
           ledger drives the stage by clicking the stage's own matching stop (one code path), and the
           stage announces every change on document as "env2:pdp:stage", which this section receives
           and repaints from WITHOUT answering back — so the two can never loop and never disagree.
  MOTION : §3.3 "ledger — the chosen row's string; the previous row's string dims to cord only". The
           <ol> is data-lamp="manual"; one IntersectionObserver lights it and the rows fade up 55 ms
           apart. Reduced motion: the core lights every lamp, manual included, with no transition.
  ARIA   : the six rows are ONE six-way choice, not six independent toggles — the <ol> carries
           role="radiogroup" and each row button role="radio" + aria-checked, so a screen reader
           hears "2 of 6" instead of six unrelated pressed states.

  Plumbing: elmsnest-v2-core (from layout/theme.liquid) supplies the tokens, fonts, .env2-* helpers,
  [data-lamp], window.env2 and the form[data-env2-buy] handler. No image is rendered here, so the
  §3.5 resolver is not needed; no background is painted (§3.1, the ground is the body's).
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign env2_p = product
  assign env2_ok = false
  if env2_p != blank and env2_p.variants.size > 0
    assign env2_ok = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if env2_ok -%}
{%- capture env2_model -%}{%- render 'elmsnest-v2-pdp-variants', product: env2_p, axis: section.settings.price_axis_option -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign FS = '~~F~~'
  assign RS = '~~R~~'
  assign env2_recs = env2_model | split: RS
  assign env2_m = env2_recs[0] | split: FS

  assign env2_mode = env2_m[1] | default: 'variants'
  assign env2_qax = env2_m[6] | plus: 0
  assign env2_qname = env2_m[7] | default: ''
  assign env2_qvals = env2_m[8] | plus: 0
  assign env2_defrow = env2_m[10] | plus: 0
  assign env2_defid = env2_m[11]
  assign env2_unit = env2_m[15] | default: ''
  assign env2_axvals = env2_m[18] | plus: 0
  assign env2_latin = '|W|w|K|k|V|A|LED|USB|'
  # units that may stand apart from the numeral as a small mark; anything else (a dimension tail such
  # as "x1.5") is joined into the numeral's own <bdi>, or RTL breaks the pair apart.
  assign env2_hunits = '|מ׳|מ|מטר|מטרים|ס״מ|יח׳|יח|יחידה|יחידות|נורות|'

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. the row list
  # Both shapes are printed by ONE loop, so the markup can never drift between them: the quantity
  # ledger is synthesised into the model's own record layout (CONTRACT-PDP §3.4) and both lists keep
  # a throw-away first record, so both are read with "offset: 1".
  assign env2_rowlist = env2_recs
  assign env2_unitone = section.settings.quantity_unit_one | default: 'יחידה'
  assign env2_unitmany = section.settings.quantity_unit | default: 'יחידות'
  if env2_mode == 'single'
    assign env2_unitprice = env2_p.price_min | plus: 0
    assign env2_unitprice_txt = env2_unitprice | money_without_currency
    assign env2_avail = '0'
    if env2_p.selected_or_first_available_variant != blank
      assign env2_avail = '1'
    endif
    assign env2_qlabel = env2_p.variants.first.title | default: ''
    if env2_qlabel == 'Default Title' or env2_qlabel == 'Title'
      assign env2_qlabel = ''
    endif
    assign env2_synth = 'skip'
    assign env2_qi = -1
    assign env2_steps = section.settings.quantity_steps | default: '1,2,3,4,6,8' | split: ','
    for env2_s in env2_steps
      assign env2_qn = env2_s | strip | plus: 0
      if env2_qn < 1
        continue
      endif
      assign env2_qi = env2_qi | plus: 1
      assign env2_tot = env2_unitprice | times: env2_qn
      if env2_qn == 1
        assign env2_qword = env2_unitone
      else
        assign env2_qword = env2_unitmany
      endif
      assign env2_per = ''
      assign env2_perlab = ''
      if env2_qn > 1
        assign env2_per = env2_unitprice_txt
        assign env2_perlab = '&#8362; ל' | append: env2_unitone
      endif
      assign env2_quiet = env2_defid | append: '^' | append: env2_qlabel | append: '^' | append: env2_unitprice | append: '^' | append: env2_avail
      assign env2_rec = 'row' | append: FS | append: env2_qi | append: FS | append: env2_qn | append: FS | append: env2_qn | append: FS | append: env2_qword | append: FS
      assign env2_rec = env2_rec | append: env2_qn | append: ' ' | append: env2_qword | append: FS | append: env2_qn | append: FS | append: '' | append: FS | append: '' | append: FS | append: '' | append: FS
      assign env2_rec = env2_rec | append: env2_tot | append: FS | append: env2_tot | append: FS | append: env2_per | append: FS | append: env2_perlab | append: FS | append: env2_avail | append: FS
      assign env2_rec = env2_rec | append: env2_defid | append: FS | append: 1 | append: FS | append: env2_quiet | append: FS | append: '' | append: FS | append: 'e'
      assign env2_synth = env2_synth | append: RS | append: env2_rec
    endfor
    assign env2_rowlist = env2_synth | split: RS
  endif

  # the money column of a synthesised record is still in cents; format it at the point of use.
  assign env2_nprinted = env2_rowlist.size | minus: 1
  assign env2_show = false
  if env2_mode == 'single' and env2_nprinted > 0
    assign env2_show = true
  elsif env2_mode != 'single' and env2_nprinted > 1
    assign env2_show = true
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. the to-scale string
  # width is the row's own first number against the widest one; the drawn bulb density is the row's
  # own bulb count, thinned so a 200-bulb string stays a string and not a bar.
  assign env2_maxn = 0
  for env2_rec in env2_rowlist offset: 1
    assign r = env2_rec | split: FS
    if r[6] != blank
      assign env2_nf = r[6] | plus: 0.0
      if env2_nf > env2_maxn
        assign env2_maxn = env2_nf
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. the head
  assign env2_words = '-|-|שני|שלושה|ארבעה|חמישה|שישה|שבעה|שמונה|תשעה|עשרה' | split: '|'
  assign env2_word = '-'
  if env2_axvals > 1 and env2_axvals < 11
    assign env2_word = env2_words[env2_axvals]
  endif
  assign env2_type = env2_p.type | default: ''
  assign env2_h1 = section.settings.heading_line1 | default: '' | strip
  if env2_h1 == ''
    if env2_mode == 'single'
      assign env2_h1 = 'כמה נקודות אור'
      if env2_type == 'תאורת שביל, עמוד וגינה'
        assign env2_h1 = env2_h1 | append: ' בדרך הביתה.'
      elsif env2_type == 'תאורת קיר'
        assign env2_h1 = env2_h1 | append: ' על הקיר.'
      elsif env2_type == 'גרילנדות ותאורה דקורטיבית'
        assign env2_h1 = env2_h1 | append: ' במרפסת.'
      elsif env2_type == 'ספוטים, פרוז׳קטורים ותאורה ניידת'
        assign env2_h1 = env2_h1 | append: ' בגינה.'
      else
        assign env2_h1 = env2_h1 | append: '.'
      endif
    elsif env2_m[3] != '0' and env2_m[3] != blank
      assign env2_h1 = 'כל שילוב והמחיר שלו.'
    elsif env2_word != '-' and env2_unit != blank and env2_unit != 'W'
      if env2_unit == 'מ׳' or env2_unit == 'מ' or env2_unit == 'מטר' or env2_unit == 'מטרים'
        assign env2_h1 = env2_word | append: ' אורכים.'
      else
        assign env2_h1 = env2_word | append: ' גדלים.'
      endif
    elsif env2_unit == 'W' and env2_word != '-'
      assign env2_h1 = env2_word | append: ' עוצמות.'
    else
      assign env2_h1 = 'כל אפשרות והמחיר שלה.'
    endif
  endif
  assign env2_h2 = section.settings.heading_line2 | default: '' | strip
  if env2_h2 == '' and env2_qvals > 1
    if env2_qname contains 'צבע'
      assign env2_h2 = 'הצבע לא משנה את המחיר.'
    elsif env2_qname != blank
      assign env2_h2 = env2_qname | append: ' לא משנה את המחיר.'
    endif
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4. the lead + the quiet sentence
  # One pass over the description's own block boundaries (strip_html glues <b>A</b><p>B</p> into "AB",
  # so the closing tags become the separators first). Everything after "פרטים שכדאי לדעת" is the spec
  # list and belongs to §4.5, not here.
  assign env2_lead = section.settings.lead | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_qdesc = section.settings.quiet_axis_desc | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_needdesc = false
  if env2_qdesc == '' and env2_qvals > 1 and env2_qax > 0
    assign env2_needdesc = true
  endif
  if env2_lead == '' or env2_needdesc
    assign env2_qvi = env2_qax | minus: 1
    assign env2_qopt = env2_p.options_with_values[env2_qvi]
    assign env2_raw = env2_p.description | replace: '</p>', '~~' | replace: '</div>', '~~' | replace: '</h1>', '~~' | replace: '</h2>', '~~' | replace: '</h3>', '~~' | replace: '</h4>', '~~' | replace: '</h5>', '~~' | replace: '</b>', '~~' | replace: '</strong>', '~~' | replace: '</li>', '~~' | replace: '</td>', '~~' | replace: '<br>', '~~' | replace: '<br/>', '~~' | replace: '<br />', '~~' | strip_html
    assign env2_blocks = env2_raw | split: '~~'
    assign env2_prev1 = ''
    assign env2_prev2 = ''
    assign env2_found = false
    for env2_b in env2_blocks
      assign env2_t = env2_b | strip
      if env2_t == ''
        continue
      endif
      if env2_t contains 'פרטים שכדאי לדעת'
        assign env2_found = true
        break
      endif
      # the quiet axis's own describing sentence: prose that names at least two of its values
      if env2_needdesc and env2_qdesc == '' and env2_t.size > 28
        assign env2_hits = 0
        for env2_v in env2_qopt.values
          if env2_v != blank and env2_t contains env2_v
            assign env2_hits = env2_hits | plus: 1
          endif
        endfor
        if env2_hits > 1
          assign env2_qdesc = env2_t
        endif
      endif
      assign env2_prev2 = env2_prev1
      assign env2_prev1 = env2_t
    endfor
    unless env2_found
      assign env2_prev1 = env2_prev2
      assign env2_prev2 = ''
    endunless
    if env2_lead == ''
      # the advice paragraph is prose, not a spec run, and it may never name a power source while
      # custom.power_source is empty (§3.7 — that is product C today).
      for env2_pass in (1..2)
        if env2_pass == 1
          assign env2_cand = env2_prev1
        else
          assign env2_cand = env2_prev2
        endif
        assign env2_okp = true
        if env2_cand.size < 25
          assign env2_okp = false
        endif
        unless env2_cand contains '.'
          assign env2_okp = false
        endunless
        if env2_cand contains ' · ' or env2_cand contains 'סולארי' or env2_cand contains 'חשמל'
          assign env2_okp = false
        endif
        if env2_okp and env2_lead == ''
          assign env2_lead = env2_cand
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif
  if env2_qdesc contains 'סולארי' or env2_qdesc contains 'חשמל'
    assign env2_qdesc = ''
  endif

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5. the quiet-axis fact line
  assign env2_qnote = section.settings.quiet_axis_note | default: '' | strip
  if env2_qnote == '' and env2_qvals > 1
    if env2_qname contains 'צבע'
      assign env2_qnote = 'אותו מחיר לכל צבע'
    else
      assign env2_qnote = 'אותו מחיר לכל ' | append: env2_qname
    endif
  endif
  assign env2_qlist = ''
  if env2_qvals > 1 and env2_qax > 0
    assign env2_qvi = env2_qax | minus: 1
    assign env2_qlist = env2_p.options_with_values[env2_qvi].values | join: ' · '
  endif

  assign env2_perlabel_over = section.settings.per_unit_suffix | default: '' | strip
  assign env2_addlabel = section.settings.add_label | default: 'הוספה לסל'
-%}
{%- if env2_show -%}
<section id="env2-pdp-ledger" data-env2-pdp-ledger class="env2-section env2-pdp-ledger" dir="rtl" style="scroll-margin-top:90px;--env2-stars:.34" aria-labelledby="env2-pdp-ledger-h2">
  <div class="env2-stars" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="env2-wrap env2-pdp-ledger__wrap">

    <div class="env2-pdp-ledger__head">
      <div class="env2-pdp-ledger__headline">
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
          <p class="env2-eyebrow env2-pdp-ledger__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        <h2 class="env2-h env2-pdp-ledger__h2" id="env2-pdp-ledger-h2">{{ env2_h1 }}{%- if env2_h2 != blank %} <em>{{ env2_h2 }}</em>{% endif -%}</h2>
      </div>
      {%- if env2_lead != blank -%}
        <p class="env2-lead env2-pdp-ledger__lead">{{ env2_lead }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <ol class="env2-pdp-ledger__rows" data-lamp="manual" data-env2-pdp-ledger-rows data-mode="{{ env2_mode }}" role="radiogroup" aria-label="{{ env2_h1 | strip_html | escape }}">
      {%- for env2_rec in env2_rowlist offset: 1 -%}
        {%- assign r = env2_rec | split: FS -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign rn = r[6]
          assign ru = r[7]
          assign rprice = r[10]
          if env2_mode == 'single'
            assign rprice = r[10] | plus: 0 | money_without_currency
          endif

          # a Latin unit shares the numeral's <bdi> so RTL can never reorder the pair ("6W");
          # a Hebrew unit stays its own <small> ("5" + "מ׳").
          assign rlatin = false
          assign rjoin = false
          assign rprobe = '|' | append: ru | append: '|'
          if ru != blank and env2_latin contains rprobe
            assign rlatin = true
          elsif ru != blank
            unless env2_hunits contains rprobe
              assign rjoin = true
            endunless
          endif
          assign rnum = rn
          if rlatin
            if ru.size > 1
              assign rnum = rn | append: ' ' | append: ru
            else
              assign rnum = rn | append: ru
            endif
          elsif rjoin
            assign rnum = rn | append: ru
          endif

          # the second label: the parsed count ("20 נורות"), else the second price axis ("אור חם 3000K").
          # A LATIN unit shares the number's own <bdi> ("96 LED"), or RTL reorders the pair to "LED 96".
          assign rcap = ''
          assign rcaplatin = false
          if r[8] != blank
            assign rcap = r[8] | append: ' ' | append: r[9]
            assign rcapprobe = '|' | append: r[9] | append: '|'
            if r[9] != blank and env2_latin contains rcapprobe
              assign rcaplatin = true
            endif
          elsif r[4] != blank
            assign rcap = r[4]
          endif

          # the to-scale string: width from this row's own number, density from its own bulb count
          assign rw = 100
          if env2_maxn > 0 and rn != blank
            assign rw = rn | times: 100.0 | divided_by: env2_maxn | round
          endif
          if rw < 14
            assign rw = 14
          endif
          if rw > 100
            assign rw = 100
          endif
          assign rdots = 0
          if env2_mode == 'single' and rn != blank
            assign rdots = rn | plus: 0
          elsif r[8] != blank
            assign rdots = r[8] | times: 1.0 | divided_by: 6.0 | round
            if rdots < 4
              assign rdots = 4
            endif
          else
            # no bulb count on this axis (a wattage row): one soft pool, not a bulb count
            assign rdots = 1
          endif
          if rdots < 1
            assign rdots = 1
          endif
          if rdots > 26
            assign rdots = 26
          endif

          # graft A: the authored caption, keyed by the option value (and optionally by handle,
          # because templates/product.elmsnest.json is shared by all 27 products)
          assign ruse = ''
          assign runit = ru
          assign rcap_over = ''
          assign rattr = ''
          assign rquiet = r[17] | split: ';'
        -%}
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign bh = block.settings.handle | default: '' | strip
            assign bv = block.settings.label | default: '' | strip
            assign bok = false
            if bv != blank and bv == r[3]
              assign bok = true
            elsif bv != blank and bv == r[2]
              assign bok = true
            endif
            if bok and bh != '' and bh != env2_p.handle
              assign bok = false
            endif
            if bok
              assign ruse = block.settings.use_caption | default: ''
              if block.settings.unit_label != blank
                assign runit = block.settings.unit_label
              endif
              if block.settings.bulbs_label != blank
                assign rcap_over = block.settings.bulbs_label
              endif
            endif
          -%}
          {%- if bok -%}{%- capture rattr -%}{{ block.shopify_attributes }}{%- endcapture -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- if rcap_over != blank -%}{%- assign rcap = rcap_over -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- unless rlatin -%}{%- assign ru = runit -%}{%- endunless -%}
        <li class="env2-pdp-ledger__row{% if forloop.index0 == env2_defrow %} env2-pdp-ledger__row--on{% endif %}" data-env2-pdp-ledger-row data-i="{{ forloop.index0 }}" data-label="{{ r[5] | escape }}" data-qty="{% if env2_mode == 'single' %}{{ r[6] }}{% else %}1{% endif %}" data-price="{{ r[11] }}" data-id="{{ r[15] }}" data-quiet="{{ r[17] | escape }}" style="--env2-pdp-ledger-d:{{ forloop.index0 }}" {{ rattr }}>
          <button type="button" class="env2-pdp-ledger__pick" data-env2-pdp-ledger-pick role="radio" aria-checked="{% if forloop.index0 == env2_defrow %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}" aria-label="{{ r[5] | escape }}, {{ rprice }} ש״ח">
            <span class="env2-pdp-ledger__n">
              {%- if rn != blank -%}
                {%- if rlatin or rjoin -%}<bdi>{{ rnum }}</bdi>{%- else -%}<bdi>{{ rn }}</bdi>{%- if ru != blank -%}<small>{{ ru }}</small>{%- endif -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="env2-pdp-ledger__n-text">{{ r[3] | escape }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <span class="env2-pdp-ledger__vis" aria-hidden="true">
              <i class="env2-pdp-ledger__string" style="--env2-pdp-ledger-w:{{ rw }}%;--env2-pdp-ledger-n:{{ rdots }}"></i>
              {%- if rcap != blank -%}<span class="env2-pdp-ledger__b">{% if rcaplatin %}<bdi>{{ rcap | escape }}</bdi>{% else %}{{ rcap | escape }}{% endif %}</span>{%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <span class="env2-pdp-ledger__use">{{ ruse }}</span>
            <span class="env2-price env2-pdp-ledger__price"><bdi>{{ rprice }}</bdi> &#8362;</span>
            <span class="env2-pdp-ledger__pm">{%- if r[12] != blank and section.settings.show_per_unit and env2_mode != 'single' -%}&#8776;&nbsp;<bdi>{{ r[12] }}</bdi> {{ env2_perlabel_over | default: r[13] }}{%- endif -%}</span>
          </button>
          <form method="post" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" accept-charset="UTF-8" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="env2-pdp-ledger__form">
            <input type="hidden" name="form_type" value="product">
            <input type="hidden" name="utf8" value="&#x2713;">
            <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="{% if env2_mode == 'single' %}{{ r[6] }}{% else %}1{% endif %}">
            {%- if rquiet.size > 1 -%}
              <select class="env2-pdp-ledger__sel" name="id" aria-label="{{ env2_qname | escape }} — {{ r[5] | escape }}">
                {%- for q in rquiet -%}
                  {%- assign qf = q | split: '^' -%}
                  <option value="{{ qf[0] }}"{% if qf[3] != '1' %} disabled{% endif %}>{{ qf[1] | escape }}</option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            {%- else -%}
              <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ r[15] }}">
            {%- endif -%}
            <button class="env2-btn env2-btn--ghost env2-btn--sm env2-pdp-ledger__add" type="submit"{% if r[14] != '1' %} disabled{% endif %}>{{ env2_addlabel }}</button>
          </form>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ol>

    {%- comment -%}
      The JS-only buy line. Under html.env2-js the six row forms above collapse into this one; with
      JS off it is display:none and the row forms are the whole path. The submit control is a
      <button> inside form[data-env2-buy], so the core posts it to /cart/add.js and opens the cart
      drawer, and §8.3 (an anchor styled as the filled pill measures 1.21:1) cannot bite.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="env2-pdp-ledger__buy" data-env2-pdp-ledger-buy>
      <span class="env2-pdp-ledger__chosen">
        <span class="env2-kicker env2-pdp-ledger__chosen-label">{{ section.settings.chosen_label | default: 'הבחירה שלכם' }}</span>
        <b class="env2-pdp-ledger__chosen-value" data-env2-pdp-ledger-mirror></b>
      </span>
      <span class="env2-price env2-pdp-ledger__buyprice" aria-live="polite"><bdi data-env2-pdp-ledger-price>{{ env2_m[12] }}</bdi> &#8362;</span>
      <form method="post" action="{{ routes.cart_add_url }}" accept-charset="UTF-8" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="env2-pdp-ledger__buyform" data-env2-buy>
        <input type="hidden" name="form_type" value="product">
        <input type="hidden" name="utf8" value="&#x2713;">
        <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ env2_defid }}" data-env2-pdp-ledger-id>
        <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1" data-env2-pdp-ledger-qty>
        {%- if env2_qvals > 1 -%}
          <select class="env2-pdp-ledger__sel env2-pdp-ledger__buysel" data-env2-pdp-ledger-quiet aria-label="{{ env2_qname | escape }}"></select>
        {%- endif -%}
        <button class="env2-btn env2-btn--sm env2-pdp-ledger__buybtn" type="submit">{{ env2_addlabel }}</button>
      </form>
    </div>

    {%- if env2_qlist != blank -%}
      <div class="env2-pdp-ledger__quiet">
        <p class="env2-kicker env2-pdp-ledger__qlabel">{{ env2_qname | escape }}</p>
        <p class="env2-pdp-ledger__qvals">{{ env2_qlist | escape }}{%- if env2_qnote != blank %} <small>{{ env2_qnote }}</small>{% endif -%}</p>
        {%- if env2_qdesc != blank -%}<p class="env2-pdp-ledger__qdesc">{{ env2_qdesc }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}
      <p class="env2-pdp-ledger__foot">{{ section.settings.footnote }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if section.settings.js_note != blank -%}
      <p class="env2-pdp-ledger__jsnote" data-env2-pdp-ledger-jsnote>{{ section.settings.js_note }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}
{%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
<section id="env2-pdp-ledger" data-env2-pdp-ledger class="env2-section env2-pdp-ledger env2-pdp-ledger--empty" dir="rtl" style="scroll-margin-top:90px">
  <div class="env2-wrap"><p class="env2-pdp-ledger__empty">מחירון הווריאנטים מופיע רק בתבנית של מוצר.</p></div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
/* ElmsNest v2 PDP §4.4 — the variant / price ledger. Rows on hairlines, never boxes (do-not §6.14 and
   §6.20: eight sections, eight compositions). No background is painted here — the ground is the
   body's (§3.1). Logical properties only; radius 0 everywhere except the core's pills. */
.env2-pdp-ledger{padding-block:clamp(72px,11vw,110px) clamp(64px,10vw,100px)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__wrap{position:relative;z-index:1}
.env2-pdp-ledger__head{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,.82fr);gap:clamp(18px,3vw,56px);align-items:end;margin-block-end:clamp(30px,4vw,54px)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__eyebrow{margin:0 0 clamp(16px,2vw,26px)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__h2{font-size:clamp(34px,4.9vw,72px)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__h2 em{display:block}
.env2-pdp-ledger__lead{margin:0;max-inline-size:42ch;padding-block-end:6px}

/* ---------- the rows ---------- */
.env2-pdp-ledger__rows{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
.env2-pdp-ledger__row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:clamp(12px,1.6vw,24px);border-block-start:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__row:last-of-type{border-block-end:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
/* Every row is its OWN grid, so a max-content column is sized per row and the price column drifted
   by a full digit between a 5-character price and a 6-character one — in the one column whose job is
   comparing six prices (TYPOGRAPHER-08). Flooring the last two columns pins the price column to the
   same x on every row, so the figures line up and tabular-nums finally pays. */
.env2-pdp-ledger__pick{flex:1 1 auto;min-inline-size:0;display:grid;
  grid-template-columns:minmax(88px,max-content) 200px minmax(0,1fr) minmax(112px,max-content) minmax(132px,max-content);
  align-items:center;column-gap:clamp(12px,1.6vw,24px);
  margin:0;padding:18px 0;border:0;border-radius:0;background:transparent;color:inherit;
  font:inherit;text-align:start;cursor:pointer;appearance:none;-webkit-appearance:none}
.env2-pdp-ledger__n{font-family:var(--env2-serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(34px,3vw,44px);line-height:1;
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--env2-ink-2);white-space:nowrap;transition:color .4s}
.env2-pdp-ledger__n small{font-size:max(12.5px,.32em);font-weight:400;margin-inline-start:.18em;letter-spacing:.02em}
.env2-pdp-ledger__n-text{font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-size:17px;font-weight:400;line-height:1.25;display:block;unicode-bidi:isolate}
.env2-pdp-ledger__vis{display:grid;gap:7px;min-inline-size:0}
/* the row's own string: length to scale, bulbs at the row's own density — drawn in CSS, so it is
   there with JS off and it cannot cost a paint. */
.env2-pdp-ledger__string{position:relative;display:block;block-size:16px;inline-size:var(--env2-pdp-ledger-w,100%)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__string::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset-inline:0;inset-block-start:7px;block-size:1px;
  background:rgba(244,238,227,.2)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__string::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset-inline:0;inset-block:0;
  background-image:radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%,rgba(255,224,178,1) 0,rgba(255,205,132,.62) 26%,rgba(255,196,110,0) 58%);
  background-size:calc(100% / var(--env2-pdp-ledger-n,10)) 100%;
  opacity:calc(.24 + .46*var(--lit,1));
  transition:opacity .55s ease;transition-delay:calc(var(--env2-pdp-ledger-d,0) * 55ms)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__b{font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:14px;line-height:1.3;color:var(--env2-mute);
  white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;unicode-bidi:isolate}
.env2-pdp-ledger__use{font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:15px;line-height:1.45;color:var(--env2-ink-2);
  text-wrap:pretty;unicode-bidi:isolate}
.env2-pdp-ledger__price{--env2-price-size:22px;color:var(--env2-ink-2);transition:color .4s,text-shadow .4s}
.env2-pdp-ledger__pm{font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:14px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--env2-mute);
  font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}
/* the chosen row: its numeral and price come up to full ink, its string lights, the others stay cord */
.env2-pdp-ledger__row--on .env2-pdp-ledger__n{color:var(--env2-ink)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__row--on .env2-pdp-ledger__price{color:var(--env2-glow);text-shadow:0 0 18px rgba(255,211,148,.3)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__row--on .env2-pdp-ledger__string::after{opacity:calc(.5 + .5*var(--lit,1));
  filter:drop-shadow(0 0 5px rgba(255,211,148,.45))}
.env2-pdp-ledger__row--on .env2-pdp-ledger__use{color:var(--env2-ink)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__pick:hover .env2-pdp-ledger__n{color:var(--env2-ink)}

/* ---------- the per-row form: the no-JS path (§4.4) ---------- */
.env2-pdp-ledger__form{flex:0 0 auto;inline-size:132px;display:grid;gap:9px;margin:0;padding:0}
.env2-pdp-ledger__sel{inline-size:100%;max-inline-size:100%;margin:0;border:0;border-block-end:1px solid var(--env2-hair-btn);
  border-radius:0;background:transparent;color:var(--env2-ink);font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:400;font-size:14px;
  line-height:1.3;padding:7px 0;min-block-size:44px;appearance:none;-webkit-appearance:none;cursor:pointer}
.env2-pdp-ledger__sel:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--env2-glow);outline-offset:3px}
.env2-pdp-ledger__sel option{background:#070b15;color:#f4eee3}
.env2-pdp-ledger__add[disabled]{opacity:.45;cursor:not-allowed}
.env2-js .env2-pdp-ledger__form{display:none}

/* ---------- the JS-only buy line (the §4.4 inversion: six forms become one) ---------- */
.env2-pdp-ledger__buy{display:none}
.env2-js .env2-pdp-ledger__buy{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:14px clamp(18px,2.4vw,34px);
  padding-block:22px;border-block-end:1px solid var(--env2-hair)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__chosen{display:grid;gap:5px;min-inline-size:0;flex:1 1 220px}
.env2-pdp-ledger__chosen-label{font-size:11.5px}
.env2-pdp-ledger__chosen-value{font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:400;font-size:16px;line-height:1.35;color:var(--env2-ink);unicode-bidi:isolate}
.env2-pdp-ledger__buyprice{--env2-price-size:26px}
.env2-pdp-ledger__buyform{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin:0;padding:0;flex-wrap:wrap}
.env2-pdp-ledger__buysel{inline-size:auto;min-inline-size:132px}
.env2-pdp-ledger__buybtn{color:var(--env2-btn-ink)}

/* ---------- the quiet axis, printed as a fact (§3.6: an axis that never changes the price) ---------- */
.env2-pdp-ledger__quiet{margin-block-start:clamp(24px,3vw,38px);display:grid;gap:7px;max-inline-size:62ch}
.env2-pdp-ledger__qlabel{margin:0;font-size:11.5px}
.env2-pdp-ledger__qvals{margin:0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:400;font-size:16px;line-height:1.4;color:var(--env2-ink);unicode-bidi:isolate}
.env2-pdp-ledger__qvals small{font-weight:300;font-size:13px;color:var(--env2-mute);margin-inline-start:.5em}
.env2-pdp-ledger__qdesc{margin:0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--env2-ink-2)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__foot{margin:clamp(22px,3vw,34px) 0 0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;font-size:14px;
  line-height:1.5;color:var(--env2-ink-2);max-inline-size:60ch}
.env2-pdp-ledger__jsnote{display:none}
.env2-js .env2-pdp-ledger__jsnote{display:block;margin:clamp(14px,2vw,20px) 0 0;font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-weight:300;
  font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--env2-mute)}
.env2-pdp-ledger__empty{font-family:var(--env2-sans);font-size:14px;color:var(--env2-mute);padding-block:40px}

/* ---------- 900px: two lines per row, never a six-column squeeze (§4.4) ---------- */
@media (max-width:900px){
  .env2-pdp-ledger{padding-block:clamp(56px,12vw,84px) clamp(48px,10vw,72px)}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__head{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);align-items:start;gap:18px}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__lead{max-inline-size:none;padding-block-end:0}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__row{display:block;padding-block:20px}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__pick{inline-size:100%;padding:0;column-gap:12px;row-gap:9px;
    grid-template-columns:auto minmax(0,1fr) auto;grid-template-areas:"n vis price" "use use pm"}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__n{grid-area:n;font-size:34px;align-self:center}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__vis{grid-area:vis;align-self:center}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__use{grid-area:use;font-size:14px;align-self:start}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__price{grid-area:price;--env2-price-size:20px;align-self:center}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__pm{grid-area:pm;justify-self:end;align-self:start;font-size:13px}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__form{inline-size:100%;margin-block-start:14px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:10px 14px}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__sel{flex:1 1 130px;inline-size:auto}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__add{flex:0 0 auto}
  .env2-js .env2-pdp-ledger__buy{gap:12px 18px;padding-block:20px}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__buyprice{--env2-price-size:24px}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__buyform{inline-size:100%}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__buybtn{flex:1 1 auto;min-block-size:48px}
}
@media (max-width:420px){
  .env2-pdp-ledger__pick{grid-template-columns:auto minmax(0,1fr) auto}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__n{font-size:30px}
  .env2-pdp-ledger__b{font-size:13px}
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% javascript %}
/* ElmsNest v2 PDP §4.4 — the ledger. Progressive enhancement only: with JS off every row is already
   visible, priced and buyable through its own form, so this file adds the selector behaviour and
   nothing the page depends on. Every number it needs is a data-* attribute Liquid already wrote on
   the row, so the section is self-sufficient — it never parses the stage's JSON tag (rendered once
   per page, by the stage) and never writes a second one. */
(function () {
  function money(n) {
    var s = (Math.round(n * 100) / 100).toFixed(2).split('.');
    return s[0].replace(/\B(?=(\d{3})+(?!\d))/g, ',') + '.' + s[1];
  }
  /* "id^label^cents^avail;id^label^cents^avail" — the row's own quiet variants (CONTRACT-PDP §3.4) */
  function parseQuiet(txt) {
    var out = [], list = (txt || '').split(';');
    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {
      if (!list[i]) { continue; }
      var f = list[i].split('^');
      out.push({ id: f[0], label: f[1] || '', price: parseInt(f[2], 10) || 0, available: f[3] === '1' });
    }
    return out;
  }

  function init(el) {
    var rows = [].slice.call(el.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-row]'));
    if (!rows.length) { return; }
    var list = el.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-rows]');
    var idEl = el.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-id]');
    var qtyEl = el.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-qty]');
    var priceEl = el.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-price]');
    var mirrorEl = el.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-mirror]');
    var quietEl = el.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-quiet]');
    var single = !!(list && list.getAttribute('data-mode') === 'single');
    var stage = document.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-stage]');
    var cur = 0;

    /* the note promises the stage lights up; if this page has no stage, the promise is not true */
    var note = el.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-jsnote]');
    if (note && !stage) { note.hidden = true; }

    var data = rows.map(function (row) {
      return {
        label: row.getAttribute('data-label') || '',
        qty: parseInt(row.getAttribute('data-qty'), 10) || 1,
        price: parseInt(row.getAttribute('data-price'), 10) || 0,
        id: row.getAttribute('data-id') || '',
        variants: parseQuiet(row.getAttribute('data-quiet'))
      };
    });
    for (var i = 0; i < rows.length; i++) {
      if (rows[i].className.indexOf('env2-pdp-ledger__row--on') > -1) { cur = i; }
    }

    function clean(v) { return (!v || v === 'Default Title' || v === 'Title') ? '' : v; }

    /* the quiet axis lives on the stage when there is one; the ledger mirrors it, and a change made
       here is pushed back, so the two can never disagree about the colour that reaches the cart. */
    function stageQuiet() {
      if (!stage) { return null; }
      return stage.querySelector('select[data-env2-stage-quiet]') ||
             stage.querySelector('input[type="radio"][data-env2-stage-quiet]:checked');
    }
    function quietText() {
      if (quietEl && quietEl.selectedIndex > -1) { return quietEl.options[quietEl.selectedIndex].text; }
      var sq = stageQuiet();
      if (sq && sq.tagName === 'SELECT' && sq.selectedIndex > -1) { return sq.options[sq.selectedIndex].text; }
      if (sq && sq.tagName === 'INPUT') { return (sq.parentNode.textContent || '').trim(); }
      return '';
    }
    function fillQuiet(d) {
      if (!quietEl) { return; }
      var keep = quietText();
      quietEl.innerHTML = '';
      for (var i = 0; i < d.variants.length; i++) {
        var o = document.createElement('option');
        o.value = d.variants[i].id; o.textContent = d.variants[i].label; o.disabled = !d.variants[i].available;
        if (d.variants[i].label === keep) { o.selected = true; }
        quietEl.appendChild(o);
      }
    }
    function chosen(d) {
      if (quietEl && quietEl.value) {
        for (var i = 0; i < d.variants.length; i++) { if (String(d.variants[i].id) === String(quietEl.value)) { return d.variants[i]; } }
      }
      for (var k = 0; k < d.variants.length; k++) { if (d.variants[k].available) { return d.variants[k]; } }
      return d.variants[0] || null;
    }

    function syncUrl(id) {
      if (!id || !window.history || !history.replaceState) { return; }
      try {
        var u = new URL(window.location.href);
        u.searchParams.set('variant', id);
        history.replaceState(null, '', u.pathname + u.search + u.hash);
      } catch (e) { /* older browser: leave the URL alone */ }
    }

    /* the stage owns the price count-up, the drawn string and the sticky bar; the ledger drives it by
       activating the stage's own matching stop, so a variant change has exactly one code path. */
    function driveStage(i, qty) {
      if (!stage) { return; }
      var stops = [].slice.call(stage.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-stage-stop]')), s = null;
      for (var k = 0; k < stops.length; k++) {
        if (single) { if (String(stops[k].getAttribute('data-qty')) === String(qty)) { s = stops[k]; } }
        else if (String(stops[k].getAttribute('data-i')) === String(i)) { s = stops[k]; }
      }
      if (s) { s.click(); }
    }

    function paint(i, fromUser) {
      cur = i;
      for (var k = 0; k < rows.length; k++) {
        var on = k === i;
        rows[k].classList.toggle('env2-pdp-ledger__row--on', on);
        var b = rows[k].querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-pick]');
        if (b) { b.setAttribute('aria-checked', on ? 'true' : 'false'); }
      }
      var d = data[i];
      if (!single) { fillQuiet(d); }
      var v = chosen(d);
      var id = (v && v.id) || d.id;
      var cents = single ? d.price : ((v && v.price) || d.price);
      if (idEl) { idEl.value = id; }
      if (qtyEl) { qtyEl.value = String(d.qty); }
      if (priceEl && cents) { priceEl.textContent = money(cents / 100); }
      if (mirrorEl) {
        var txt = d.label;
        var q = clean(single ? '' : quietText());
        if (q) { txt = txt ? (txt + ' · ' + q) : q; }
        mirrorEl.textContent = txt;
      }
      if (fromUser) { driveStage(i, d.qty); syncUrl(id); }
    }

    rows.forEach(function (row, i) {
      var btn = row.querySelector('[data-env2-pdp-ledger-pick]');
      if (btn) { btn.addEventListener('click', function () { paint(i, true); }); }
      /* the whole row is a target, but never at the cost of the row's own form controls */
      row.addEventListener('click', function (ev) {
        if (ev.target && ev.target.closest && ev.target.closest('form,select,button,a')) { return; }
        paint(i, true);
      });
    });
    if (quietEl) {
      quietEl.addEventListener('change', function () {
        var want = quietEl.selectedIndex > -1 ? quietEl.options[quietEl.selectedIndex].text : '';
        var sq = stageQuiet();
        if (sq && sq.tagName === 'SELECT' && want) {
          for (var k = 0; k < sq.options.length; k++) {
            if (sq.options[k].text === want) { sq.selectedIndex = k; break; }
          }
          try { sq.dispatchEvent(new Event('change', { bubbles: true })); } catch (e) { /* old Event(): nothing to sync */ }
        }
        paint(cur, false);
        syncUrl(quietEl.value);
      });
    }

    /* SHOPPER-01: the binding is TWO-WAY. driveStage() sends a ledger pick up to the stage; this
       receives the stage's own picks (the fold rail, the colour select, the radio line) and repaints
       the ledger from them, so the row marked "your choice" and the id its buy line posts can never
       disagree with the price at the top of the page. paint(i,false) does not call driveStage, so the
       two directions cannot loop. */
    document.addEventListener('env2:pdp:stage', function (ev) {
      var d = (ev && ev.detail) || {};
      if (!d.stage || d.stage !== stage) { return; }
      if (quietEl && d.quiet) {
        for (var q = 0; q < quietEl.options.length; q++) {
          if (quietEl.options[q].text === d.quiet) { quietEl.selectedIndex = q; break; }
        }
      }
      var want = -1;
      if (single) {
        for (var k = 0; k < data.length; k++) { if (String(data[k].qty) === String(d.qty)) { want = k; } }
      } else if (typeof d.row === 'number' && d.row > -1 && d.row < rows.length) {
        want = d.row;
      }
      if (want < 0 || want === cur) {
        if (want === cur) { paint(cur, false); }
        return;
      }
      paint(want, false);
    });

    /* an incoming ?variant= (a shared link, a Meta catalogue deep link) opens on its own row */
    var start = cur;
    try {
      var want = new URL(window.location.href).searchParams.get('variant');
      if (want && !single) {
        for (var a = 0; a < data.length; a++) {
          for (var b2 = 0; b2 < data[a].variants.length; b2++) {
            if (String(data[a].variants[b2].id) === String(want)) { start = a; }
          }
        }
      }
    } catch (e) { /* no URL support: keep the server's default row */ }
    paint(start, false);

    /* §3.3: the rows light on arrival, 55 ms apart (the delay is a CSS custom property on each row) */
    if (list) {
      var lit = false;
      var lightAll = function () {
        if (lit) { return; }
        lit = true;
        if (window.env2 && env2.light) { env2.light(list); } else { list.classList.add('lit'); }
      };
      var rm = window.env2 ? env2.rm : false;
      if (rm || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) { lightAll(); }
      else {
        var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
          for (var n = 0; n < entries.length; n++) {
            if (entries[n].isIntersecting) { io.disconnect(); lightAll(); return; }
          }
        }, { threshold: 0.25, rootMargin: '0px 0px -6% 0px' });
        io.observe(list);
      }
    }
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('[data-env2-pdp-ledger]').forEach(function (el) {
    init(el);
    window.env2 ? env2.observe(el) : el.querySelectorAll('[data-lamp]').forEach(function (l) { l.classList.add('lit'); });
  });
})();
{% endjavascript %}

